    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d573">

                <pb facs="0993" n="889" xml:id="pg889"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0019 PW 1939/8–1145: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hurley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Byrnes</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-08-11">August 11, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1330.… The Generalissimo has mentioned to me frequently President Roosevelt’s
                    statement at Cairo to the effect that the United States would equip ninety
                    Chinese divisions. Thirty divisions (X force) to be equipped immediately. Thirty
                    divisions (Y force) as soon as first thirty divisions were completed and finally
                    the arming of thirty additional divisions (Z force) making a total of ninety
                    American armed divisions which would constitute the Chinese peacetime army.</p>
                <p>Chiang Kai-Shek said Harry Hopkins was present when commitment was made.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
            </div>
        </body>
